{
 "measurement": "scripts/check_propagated_exclusions.py --evidence nearest --calibrate",
 "date": "2026-08-28",
 "question": "910 sentences were withheld from Dictation on instrument 2's 'nearest hypothesis' verdict. v1.26 measured that instrument at 42/63 = 67% agreement with adjudication on this very population, with a median margin LARGER when it is wrong (0.0240) than when it is right (0.0177) — a margin that grows when the instrument errs is not evidence. PLAN-V1.27 recorded that re-deciding them 'needs an instrument this repo does not have'. Instrument 1b is that instrument.",
 "result": {
  "released": 161,
  "provenMisread": 227,
  "undecided": 522
 },
 "dictationPool": {
  "before": 5770,
  "after": 5931
 },
 "calibration": {
  "negativeControl": "1,816 decoy substitutions -> 0 spurious byte matches.",
  "positiveControl": "39 sentences instrument 1 had already proven -> 1b contradicts 0.",
  "rebuildIdentity": "910/910 (string handling only; no linguistic weight)."
 },
 "theDefectThisRunFound": "The release predicate was RIGHT for the population it was written against and SILENTLY VACUOUS on this one. It required the DISPUTED word to be confirmed, taking 'disputed' from one global set built out of the rows whose evidence begins 'proven'. That is correct for the `propagated` class, which inherited a verdict about one of THOSE words. Every `nearest` row carries its own complaint instead ('紙 かみ -> がみ'), none of which is in that set — so for 382 of 388 releases the coverage check was skipped entirely and the sentence was released on whatever unrelated span happened to agree. Fixed to read each row's own complaint: RELEASE fell from 388 to 161, and 236 sentences that would have shipped carried a real, never-confirmed complaint (別 べつ->べち, 古い ふるい->ふりい, 家 いえ->け, 明日 あす->あした). A predicate that is right for one population and vacuous on another is this project's oldest shape wearing a population instead of a call site.",
 "whatSilenceMeans": "523 sentences stay withheld because instrument 1b said NOTHING about them. That is not a verdict. They were withheld by an instrument known to be near-uninformative on this population, so remaining withheld is not a safe default either — it is an invisible one. Released, kept and undecided are reported as three numbers and never collapsed into two.",
 "evidenceUpgrade": "226 sentences moved from instrument 2's 67%-accurate 'nearest' verdict to PROOF that they are read differently from their answer key. Those were withheld correctly, and now they are withheld for a reason that can be checked.",
