 "whyTheSilenceCannotBeChasedFurther": "Instrument 2 named a specific hypothesis for every one of these sentences ('紙 かみ -> がみ'), and the obvious next move was to make sure 1b always tests it — an instrument that declines to test the hypothesis it was pointed at cannot report on it. Measured before implementing: Sudachi ALREADY proposed that hypothesis for 518 of the 523 silent sentences, and testing the remaining 5 converted exactly ONE (n2-b243, 消しゴム けしごむ -> けしゴム) and released none. So the silence is not a coverage gap that a longer candidate list closes. It is instrument 1b's recall limit: substituting kana at a span changes prosody, so neither the corpus reading nor the complaint renders byte-identically, and byte identity has nothing to say. Moving these 522 needs a DIFFERENT instrument, not a more thorough version of this one — and this repo does not have one. AVSpeechSynthesisMarker's phoneme marks are empty for every Japanese voice and NSSpeechSynthesizer.phonemes returns empty even for English, both checked in v1.21."
}
